## 📁 6. Core Project Structure

```text
/hybrid_Anime_Recommendation_System
├── .github/          # (Optional) GitHub templates
├── .dvc/             # Data Version Control configuration & remotes
├── artifacts/        # [DVC Tracked] ML Models, encoders, & processed dataframes
├── config/           # Centralized configuration (paths, model hyperparameters)
├── frontend/         # React Application
│   ├── src/          # React components, styles, and utilities
│   │   ├── utils/    # Contains posterFetcher.js checking AniList & Jikan
│   ├── dist/         # (Generated) Production build output used by Flask
│   └── vite.config.js
├── pipelines/        # Model prediction & training pipeline logic
├── src/              # Raw data processing and model architecture source code
├── utils/            # Helper scripts (e.g., getting anime metadata)
├── app.py            # Main Flask Entrypoint (API & Static File Server)
├── Dockerfile        # Multi-stage build manifest for GCP
├── deployment.yaml   # Kubernetes configuration (Deployments + LoadBalancer)
├── Jenkinsfile       # The pipeline logic executed by the Jenkins orchestrator
└── requirements.txt  # Python package list
```

---

## 🔌 7. Main API Endpoints

- **`GET /api/health`:** Readiness probe check used explicitly by GKE to know if a given pod is safe to receive traffic (waiting for large TF models to load).
- **`GET /api/search?q={text}`:** Fast autocomplete searching possible anime titles bounding to user input.
- **`POST /api/recommend`:** The primary workhorse endpoint. Resolves an `anime_name` alongside configurable weight biases to output 10 hybrid recommendations.
- **`GET /api/anime/{name}`:** Fetches detailed metadata for a single anime.

Welcome to the team, and happy coding! 🚀

